{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waffleY"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waffleX"},{"type":"text","value":" divide nonnegative source values into equal visual\nunits. They pack directly inside the final chart bounds, so no positional\nscales or application-owned cell expansion are required."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { waffleX, waffleY } from '@tanstack/charts/waffle'\n\nconst mark = waffleY(rows, {\n  y: 'share',\n  color: 'category',\n  unit: 0.01,\n  round: true,\n  gap: 2,\n  radius: 2,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both marks are also exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/universal"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"orientation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Orientation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waffleY"},{"type":"text","value":" treats "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"},{"type":"text","value":" as each source row's contribution. Units advance\nleft-to-right, then bottom-to-top. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waffleX"},{"type":"text","value":" transposes the contract: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"},{"type":"text","value":"\ncontains the contribution and units advance bottom-to-top, then left-to-right."}]},{"type":"code","value":"function waffleY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: WaffleYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum, ChartKey, number, never, never>\n\nfunction waffleX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: WaffleXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum, number, ChartKey, never, never>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"WaffleOptions<TDatum>"},{"type":"text","value":" contains the shared identity, unit, paint, state, and\nmotion fields. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"WaffleYOptions<TDatum>"},{"type":"text","value":" adds "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columns"},{"type":"text","value":";\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"WaffleXOptions<TDatum>"},{"type":"text","value":" adds "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rows"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, number?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required by Y"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contribution encoded by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waffleY"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, number?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required by X"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contribution encoded by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waffleX"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unit"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Semantic value represented by one complete cell"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"round"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Round cumulative unit boundaries before allocating cells"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columns"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsive"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fixed cells per row for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waffleY"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rows"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsive"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fixed cells per column for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waffleX"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gap"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Empty pixels between complete cells"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"radius"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Corner radius for complete cells"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layer-derived"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable mark ID"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No group"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interaction group; color fallback when omitted"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"color"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Value sent to the chart color scale"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inferred"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable source-row identity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fill"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stroke"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel<TDatum, string>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resolved color"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-row paint overrides"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fillOpacity"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeOpacity"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeWidth"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renderer default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cell presentation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"states"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"readonly ChartMarkState[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focus-driven rectangle styles applied to every source tile"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkMotionOptions<TDatum>['motion']"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-tile motion policy"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unit"},{"type":"text","value":" must be positive and finite. Contributions must be nonnegative and\nfinite; nullish and nonfinite channel values are omitted. Fixed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columns"},{"type":"text","value":" or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rows"},{"type":"text","value":" must be positive integers, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gap"},{"type":"text","value":" must be nonnegative."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"unit-boundaries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unit boundaries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The mark allocates each row against cumulative values. With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unit: 0.01"},{"type":"text","value":", a\ncomplete cell represents one percentage point. With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"round: true"},{"type":"text","value":", cumulative\nboundaries are rounded, so the complete allocation preserves the rounded total\nwithout independently rounding every category."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"round"},{"type":"text","value":" is false, a category boundary may divide one cell. Each category\nreceives its exact fractional rectangle and the adjacent fragments meet without\nan added gap. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"radius"},{"type":"text","value":" applies only to complete cells."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"responsive-packing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsive packing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Without "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columns"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rows"},{"type":"text","value":", the mark chooses a square-cell grid from the final\nplot bounds after margins and legends resolve. It may change the number of rows\nor columns when the chart resizes while preserving source order and keys. Set\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columns"},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waffleY"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rows"},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waffleX"},{"type":"text","value":" when the grid count is part of the\nchart's meaning, such as a fixed ten-by-ten percentage display."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"source-identity-and-interaction","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source identity and interaction"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cell expansion is internal. Each visible source row contributes one interaction\npoint, and every complete or fractional tile for that row references the same\noriginal datum and datum index. The quantitative point value remains the row's\ncontribution; cumulative start and end values are exposed as its interval."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Color-domain inference uses the original source rows, including a category that\nrounds to zero visible cells. This keeps an explicitly meaningful category in a\nlegend without manufacturing a rendered interaction point."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"orientation","text":"Orientation","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"unit-boundaries","text":"Unit boundaries","level":2},{"id":"responsive-packing","text":"Responsive packing","level":2},{"id":"source-identity-and-interaction","text":"Source identity and interaction","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`waffleY` and `waffleX` divide nonnegative source values into equal visual\nunits. They pack directly inside the final chart bounds, so no positional\nscales or application-owned cell expansion are required.\n\n```ts\nimport { waffleX, waffleY } from '@tanstack/charts/waffle'\n\nconst mark = waffleY(rows, {\n  y: 'share',\n  color: 'category',\n  unit: 0.01,\n  round: true,\n  gap: 2,\n  radius: 2,\n})\n```\n\nBoth marks are also exported from `@tanstack/charts` and\n`@tanstack/charts/universal`.\n\n## Orientation\n\n`waffleY` treats `y` as each source row's contribution. Units advance\nleft-to-right, then bottom-to-top. `waffleX` transposes the contract: `x`\ncontains the contribution and units advance bottom-to-top, then left-to-right.\n\n```ts\nfunction waffleY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: WaffleYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum, ChartKey, number, never, never>\n\nfunction waffleX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: WaffleXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum, number, ChartKey, never, never>\n```\n\n## Options\n\n`WaffleOptions<TDatum>` contains the shared identity, unit, paint, state, and\nmotion fields. `WaffleYOptions<TDatum>` adds `y` and `columns`;\n`WaffleXOptions<TDatum>` adds `x` and `rows`.\n\n| Option                                            | Type                                       | Default          | Meaning                                                    |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `y`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, number?>`                 | Required by Y    | Contribution encoded by `waffleY`                          |\n| `x`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, number?>`                 | Required by X    | Contribution encoded by `waffleX`                          |\n| `unit`                                            | `number`                                   | `1`              | Semantic value represented by one complete cell            |\n| `round`                                           | `boolean`                                  | `false`          | Round cumulative unit boundaries before allocating cells   |\n| `columns`                                         | `number`                                   | Responsive       | Fixed cells per row for `waffleY`                          |\n| `rows`                                            | `number`                                   | Responsive       | Fixed cells per column for `waffleX`                       |\n| `gap`                                             | `number`                                   | `1`              | Empty pixels between complete cells                        |\n| `radius`                                          | `number`                                   | None             | Corner radius for complete cells                           |\n| `id`                                              | `string`                                   | Layer-derived    | Stable mark ID                                             |\n| `z`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`               | No group         | Interaction group; color fallback when omitted             |\n| `color`                                           | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`               | `z`              | Value sent to the chart color scale                        |\n| `key`                                             | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`                | Inferred         | Stable source-row identity                                 |\n| `fill`, `stroke`                                  | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`            | Resolved color   | Per-row paint overrides                                    |\n| `fillOpacity`, `strokeOpacity`, and `strokeWidth` | `number`                                   | Renderer default | Cell presentation                                          |\n| `states`                                          | `readonly ChartMarkState[]`                | None             | Focus-driven rectangle styles applied to every source tile |\n| `motion`                                          | `ChartMarkMotionOptions<TDatum>['motion']` | None             | Per-tile motion policy                                     |\n\n`unit` must be positive and finite. Contributions must be nonnegative and\nfinite; nullish and nonfinite channel values are omitted. Fixed `columns` or\n`rows` must be positive integers, and `gap` must be nonnegative.\n\n## Unit boundaries\n\nThe mark allocates each row against cumulative values. With `unit: 0.01`, a\ncomplete cell represents one percentage point. With `round: true`, cumulative\nboundaries are rounded, so the complete allocation preserves the rounded total\nwithout independently rounding every category.\n\nWhen `round` is false, a category boundary may divide one cell. Each category\nreceives its exact fractional rectangle and the adjacent fragments meet without\nan added gap. `radius` applies only to complete cells.\n\n## Responsive packing\n\nWithout `columns` or `rows`, the mark chooses a square-cell grid from the final\nplot bounds after margins and legends resolve. It may change the number of rows\nor columns when the chart resizes while preserving source order and keys. Set\n`columns` on `waffleY` or `rows` on `waffleX` when the grid count is part of the\nchart's meaning, such as a fixed ten-by-ten percentage display.\n\n## Source identity and interaction\n\nCell expansion is internal. Each visible source row contributes one interaction\npoint, and every complete or fractional tile for that row references the same\noriginal datum and datum index. The quantitative point value remains the row's\ncontribution; cumulative start and end values are exposed as its interval.\n\nColor-domain inference uses the original source rows, including a category that\nrounds to zero visible cells. This keeps an explicitly meaningful category in a\nlegend without manufacturing a rendered interaction point.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Waffle Marks\ndescription: Reference for responsive waffleY and waffleX unit layouts, cumulative rounding, color, source identity, and interaction.\n---\n\n`waffleY` and `waffleX` divide nonnegative source values into equal visual\nunits. They pack directly inside the final chart bounds, so no positional\nscales or application-owned cell expansion are required.\n\n```ts\nimport { waffleX, waffleY } from '@tanstack/charts/waffle'\n\nconst mark = waffleY(rows, {\n  y: 'share',\n  color: 'category',\n  unit: 0.01,\n  round: true,\n  gap: 2,\n  radius: 2,\n})\n```\n\nBoth marks are also exported from `@tanstack/charts` and\n`@tanstack/charts/universal`.\n\n## Orientation\n\n`waffleY` treats `y` as each source row's contribution. Units advance\nleft-to-right, then bottom-to-top. `waffleX` transposes the contract: `x`\ncontains the contribution and units advance bottom-to-top, then left-to-right.\n\n```ts\nfunction waffleY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: WaffleYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum, ChartKey, number, never, never>\n\nfunction waffleX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: WaffleXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum, number, ChartKey, never, never>\n```\n\n## Options\n\n`WaffleOptions<TDatum>` contains the shared identity, unit, paint, state, and\nmotion fields. `WaffleYOptions<TDatum>` adds `y` and `columns`;\n`WaffleXOptions<TDatum>` adds `x` and `rows`.\n\n| Option                                            | Type                                       | Default          | Meaning                                                    |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `y`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, number?>`                 | Required by Y    | Contribution encoded by `waffleY`                          |\n| `x`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, number?>`                 | Required by X    | Contribution encoded by `waffleX`                          |\n| `unit`                                            | `number`                                   | `1`              | Semantic value represented by one complete cell            |\n| `round`                                           | `boolean`                                  | `false`          | Round cumulative unit boundaries before allocating cells   |\n| `columns`                                         | `number`                                   | Responsive       | Fixed cells per row for `waffleY`                          |\n| `rows`                                            | `number`                                   | Responsive       | Fixed cells per column for `waffleX`                       |\n| `gap`                                             | `number`                                   | `1`              | Empty pixels between complete cells                        |\n| `radius`                                          | `number`                                   | None             | Corner radius for complete cells                           |\n| `id`                                              | `string`                                   | Layer-derived    | Stable mark ID                                             |\n| `z`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`               | No group         | Interaction group; color fallback when omitted             |\n| `color`                                           | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`               | `z`              | Value sent to the chart color scale                        |\n| `key`                                             | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`                | Inferred         | Stable source-row identity                                 |\n| `fill`, `stroke`                                  | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`            | Resolved color   | Per-row paint overrides                                    |\n| `fillOpacity`, `strokeOpacity`, and `strokeWidth` | `number`                                   | Renderer default | Cell presentation                                          |\n| `states`                                          | `readonly ChartMarkState[]`                | None             | Focus-driven rectangle styles applied to every source tile |\n| `motion`                                          | `ChartMarkMotionOptions<TDatum>['motion']` | None             | Per-tile motion policy                                     |\n\n`unit` must be positive and finite. Contributions must be nonnegative and\nfinite; nullish and nonfinite channel values are omitted. Fixed `columns` or\n`rows` must be positive integers, and `gap` must be nonnegative.\n\n## Unit boundaries\n\nThe mark allocates each row against cumulative values. With `unit: 0.01`, a\ncomplete cell represents one percentage point. With `round: true`, cumulative\nboundaries are rounded, so the complete allocation preserves the rounded total\nwithout independently rounding every category.\n\nWhen `round` is false, a category boundary may divide one cell. Each category\nreceives its exact fractional rectangle and the adjacent fragments meet without\nan added gap. `radius` applies only to complete cells.\n\n## Responsive packing\n\nWithout `columns` or `rows`, the mark chooses a square-cell grid from the final\nplot bounds after margins and legends resolve. It may change the number of rows\nor columns when the chart resizes while preserving source order and keys. Set\n`columns` on `waffleY` or `rows` on `waffleX` when the grid count is part of the\nchart's meaning, such as a fixed ten-by-ten percentage display.\n\n## Source identity and interaction\n\nCell expansion is internal. Each visible source row contributes one interaction\npoint, and every complete or fractional tile for that row references the same\noriginal datum and datum index. The quantitative point value remains the row's\ncontribution; cumulative start and end values are exposed as its interval.\n\nColor-domain inference uses the original source rows, including a category that\nrounds to zero visible cells. This keeps an explicitly meaningful category in a\nlegend without manufacturing a rendered interaction point.\n"}
